{"body":{"text":["What Unix did right was unify things: every program stood on one floor of files and text. Since then programs have become worlds of their own, each with its data shut inside, and our files went into the cloud. Between the worlds people build glue, and AI is mostly put to gluing them faster. Glass begins again from one field. A part of it may still be kept apart, by choice, but nothing in how it is built divides it. Unix made everything a file; glass makes everything a holon. *Proposed, 2026-11-24.*"]},"id":"1M86DQSKWR12000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**recreating field:** what glass is, as an operating system is what Unix is: one field that everything acts through, whose purpose is creating anew from what it holds, what is created becoming more of what it holds, nothing lost."]},"id":"1M86DQSKWR12001","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**holonic field:** the level beneath, as a file system is beneath Unix: a field whose every part is a holon."]},"id":"1M86DQSKWR12002","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**re-member:** what a reference that holds does: it keeps a part a member of every whole it stands in, never a copy."]},"id":"1M86DQSKWR12003","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**statement:** a commit as its maker's act: what was chosen, kept with what had been read."]},"id":"1M86DQSKWR12004","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
