{"body":{"text":["Glass is a working name. What glass is to be called is open: a name that says what it is as operating system says what Unix is, and that can be held as a mark for software."]},"id":"1M86DQSKWR12008","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The measure a session drew with the author: the name names the core, the field and its purpose, creating anew from what it holds with nothing lost, and not a piece of it. It is one word, and where it is made, it is made as holon was, two words each giving up part of itself rather than set side by side. It is plain: no sideways metaphor, no word of the wrong kind, no theme the ontology does not hold. Common words are no fault; a mark already held for software is."]},"id":"1M86DQSKWR12009","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What the search taught: a word for the purpose tends to miss the medium, and a word for the medium misses the purpose. English joins the two in few ways: re- on a word for the medium, -en, to make, on a word for the whole, and -ium, the ending of medium, on a word for the purpose. The truest word met was the purpose itself, re-creating, and as a name it is held for software by another."]},"id":"1M86DQSKWR1200A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The names weighed are kept apart from the published field, so that naming them here does not invite their domains to be taken first. *Open: whether the name is found first by its meaning or by its sound.*"]},"id":"1M86DQSKWR1200B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
